SQL Injection UNION Attack – Retrieving Data from Other Tables

Vulnerability: SQL Injection
 Difficulty: Practitioner
 Platform: PortSwigger Web Security Academy

Goal

Retrieve usernames and passwords from the users table and log in as administrator.

Steps I Followed

Opened the lab and tested the category filter.

Added a single quote (') in the category parameter and got an Internal Server Error.

This confirmed that the category filter was vulnerable to SQL injection.

The lab description already mentioned a table called users with columns username and password.

I used the following payload in the category filter:

SQL
' UNION SELECT username, password FROM users--
The application displayed the user credentials:
Plain Text
carlos fmxsd020t3eqagxe2154
administrator 886zpueempw16t343in5
wiener hdom2ffrbjc1t93fs53r

I copied the administrator credentials and logged in.

After logging in as administrator, the lab was solved.

Impact

An attacker could use SQL injection to read data from other tables and steal sensitive information such as usernames and passwords.

What I Learned
How to confirm SQL injection using '.
How to use a UNION attack to retrieve data from another table.
How to extract usernames and passwords from the database.
How exposed credentials can lead to account compromise.
